hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6436","On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and Jabir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Truffles are part of manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6437","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Abu Khaythamah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Iyas, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Saeed and Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Truffles are part of manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” The disagreement over Suleiman Al-A’mash (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6438","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Shahr, and Abu Nadra told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, On the authority of Jabir, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day with truffles in his hand, and he said: “This is manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6439","Ahmad bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us with truffles in his hand, and he said: “These are of manna, and their water is healing.” \For the damned\"""""""
"6440","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ata bin Abi told me. Rabah, that Jabir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever eats garlic or onions, let him isolate us. “And let him withdraw from our mosque and sit at home.”"
"6441","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ziyad Khayyar bin Salamah, that he asked Aisha about Onions, and she said: “The last food that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate was food that contained onions.”"
"6442","Harun bin Zaid bin Abi Al-Zarqa told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Khalid bin Maysarah told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Qurrah told us, on the authority of his father Qurrah. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever eats from these two evil trees should not approach our mosque, for if you must eat them, then kill them by cooking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6443","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Shababah bin Suwar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha, said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “You eat from two trees that I do not see as anything but evil: garlic, And onions, if the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded a man to have their scent emanating from him, and to take him out to Al-Baqi’, so whoever Whoever among you eats them, it is inevitable, let him kill them by cooking them.” Husayn and Mansour opposed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6444","Suleiman bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: Omar said: “Beware of food. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated garlic and onions, so whoever wants to eat them should not eat them until he kills them when they are ripe.”"
"6445","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: Omar said: “You are eating food “These two trees are evil: the onion and the garlic. If you eat them, then kill them when they are ripe.”"
"6446","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Jabir, narrating, that the Messenger prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever eats from this herb, the garlic, should not deceive us in our mosques, for the angels are harmed by what is harmed.” “thereby the Muslim” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6447","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever eats from this tree and says for the first time: garlic, then says: garlic, onions, and leeks, should not bring it near us.” Our mosques, for the angels are harmed by whatever people are harmed by.”"
"6448","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Abdul-Malik, who is Ibn Jurayj, told us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade leeks, but they did not stop eating them, and they did not find anyone who ate them to feel their smell.” He said: Did I not forbid you from eating it? Whoever eats it should not deceive us in our mosques, for angels are harmed by what humans are harmed by. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6449","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ata bin Abi told me Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought something, and he said another time: A pot containing two green of legumes, and he found a smell in them, so he asked them, and he was informed of the legumes that were in them, so he said: “Bring them to some of his companions who were with him, so when He saw that he disliked eating it, so he said: “Eat, for I will communicate with someone whom you do not communicate with.”"
"6450","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab, he said: I heard Talha bin Nafi’ Abu Sufyan, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How good is vinegar.”"
"6451","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Samit, on the authority of Abu He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you make broth, add more water to it, then look at the house of one of your neighbors. So show them kindness from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6452","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir said: “Ali came from Yemen with a gift for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was the gift that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought.” He and Ali brought one hundred camels from Yemen, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered sixty-three of them, and Ali slaughtered thirty-seven. He joined Ali in his body, then he took a small portion from each body, put it in a pot, and cooked it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate. He and Ali were greeted with some of its meat, and they drank from its broth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6453","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Husayn al-Ju’fi told us, he said: Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman al-Ansari, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over food.”"
"6454","Nasir bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Talbinah is comforting to the sick person’s heart and takes away some of the sadness,” on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Naim, on the authority of Hibban bin Musa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6455","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Asim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me and said: “Do you have anything?” I said: No. He said: I am fasting. She said: Then He passed by me after that day, and Hais had been given to us as a gift yesterday, and I had hidden some for him, and he loved Hais. She said: O Messenger of God, Hays was given to us as a gift, so I have hidden some of it for you. He said: Bring it closer, but I have woken up fasting.”"
"6456","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Salama bin Abdul-Rahman. On the authority of Ya’ish ibn Takhfa al-Ghifari, he said: My father was one of the people of the Suffah, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to go. With the man, and the man went with the two men, until five people remained, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Go,” so we went. He took him to Aisha's house, and he said: O Aisha, feed us. She brought a group of animals, and we ate. Then she brought a group of animals like cats. So we ate, then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink, so she brought a cup, so we drank. Then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink, so she brought a small cup. Of milk, so we drank, then he said: If you wish, you may complete the prayer, and if you wish, you may go to the mosque. We said: No, rather we will go to the mosque. Al-Awza’i disagreed with him. Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, he said: I am my father, he said: I am Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said Ibn Luqis bin Takhfah told me on the authority of his father, who was one of the people of the Suffah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to us after Morocco, so he says: “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so... He cited the hadith. Al-Walid ibn Muslim disagreed with him. Mahmoud ibn Khalid told us, He said: Al-Walid narrated to us. He said: Abu Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Qays bin Takhfah Al-Ghafari, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. Peace be upon him, while we were in Suffah after dinner (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6457","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Jurayj told us, he said: Ismail bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Asim Bin Laqit bin Sabra, on the authority of his father Laqit, who said: We followed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we did not find him, so she sent to us Aisha with porridge and dates, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and said: “Have you eaten anything?” We said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6458","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Sa’id, who is the son of Qattan told us, he said: Yahya bin Sa’id, who is Al-Ansari told us, he said: Tell me Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Suwayd bin Al-Nu’man, who was one of the people of the tree, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among the red-haired ones, so he called With food, so we brought a stalk, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate it, then he got up and prayed, but he did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6459","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “My aunt gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a gift of aqat, ghee, and a lizard. He ate some of the aqat and ghee, and left the lizard.” It was filthy, and it was eaten at the table of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if it had been forbidden, it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6460","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Our father told us, he said: Hassan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of a man from Al-Ansar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat this oil and anoint yourself with it, for it is from a blessed tree.”"
"6461","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, he said: Ataa, a man who was It will be on the coast, on the authority of Abu Usayd, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Eat oil and anoint yourself with it, for it is from a blessed tree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6462","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told me, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, admired her beauty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6463","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Usama, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loves honey and sweets.”"
"6464","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that a man He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Is my brother complaining about his stomach?” So he said: “Give him honey to drink.” So he gave it to him, and he said: I gave him something to drink, but it only increased it. Absolutely, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has told the truth, and your brother’s stomach has lied. Shayban bin Abdul Rahman disagreed with him in his chain of transmission. And its text (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6465","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Shayban told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My nephew’s stomach has run out, so he said: “Give your nephew a drink.” Honey, and he made him drink it, but it only made him more distressed, so he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, three times, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him when Third: Give your nephew a drink of honey, for God has told the truth, and your nephew’s stomach has lied. So he gave him something to drink, and may God forgive him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6466","On the authority of Ahmad ibn Bakkar, on the authority of Bishr ibn al-Sari, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu al-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his mother Amra On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A house you do not pass through, its people are hungry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6467","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of her uncle Salman bin Amir, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of this. He said: “If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates, for that is a blessing. “Water, for it is pure.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: We do not know that anyone mentioned in this hadith: It is a blessing, other than Sufyan (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6468","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham Basri told me, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of Salman bin Amir, he said: “If one of you is fasting, let him break his fast with dates. If he cannot find dates, let him break his fast with water, for water is purification.” Hisham said: Asim Al-Ahwal told me this hadith, attributing it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6469","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Salman bin Amir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not find dates, let him break his fast with water, for it purifies them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6470","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Abu Qutaibah told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not find them, let him break his fast with water, for \purified\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6471","Muhammad bin Umar bin Ali bin Muqaddam told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not, let him break his fast with water, for it is pure.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a mistake, and we do not know that anyone followed Saeed bin Amir on this chain of transmission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6472","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Shuja’ bin al-Walid, on the authority of Hashim, and Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Mansour, he said: Ibrahim bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever eats seven Ajwa dates in the morning, neither poison nor magic will harm him that day.” Ishaq said in his hadith: This means that day. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6473","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Khalid bin Mukhlid told me, on the authority of Sulaiman, he said: Sharik bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Abi Atiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is a cure in a high ajwa, or it is An antidote, early morning on an empty stomach.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6474","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Al-Hilal told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Abu Khaythamah told us, he said: Sulayman Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Saeed, and Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Ajwa is from Paradise, and it is \cure from poison\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6475","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Shahr, he said: Abu Nadra told me, on the authority of my father Saeed, and on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The ajwa is from Paradise, and it is a cure for poison.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6476","Muhammad ibn Bashhar informed us in his hadith, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, who said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Ajwa is from Paradise, and it is a cure for poison.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6477","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of my father Kitten, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The ajwa is from Paradise, and it is a cure for poison.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Abi Arouba entered within a month, and Abu Hurairah explained: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6478","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ajwa is from Paradise, and it is a cure for poison.”"
"6479","Ahmad bin Al-Khalil Baghdadi told us, I wrote about him in Nishapur, he said: Zakaria bin Adi told us, he said: I am Ibrahim bin Humaid Al-Rawasi. On the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to eat dates with watermelon,” on the authority of Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i Al-Saffar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hisham, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, with whom Dawud disagreed Al-Tai (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6480","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, meaning Ibn Mansour, he said: Dawood told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us May God bless him and grant him peace, “He combined watermelon and fresh dates together.”"
"6481","Muhammad bin Umar bin Ali bin Ata bin Muqaddam informed us, saying: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Qays told me, saying: I heard Hisham bin Urwa He mentions on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat dates with dates, for when the son of Adam eats them Satan became angry and said: The son of Adam lived until creation was devoured with the new. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6482","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me, they treated me with nothing. So they fed me cucumbers with dates, and I became fat on them like the best fat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6483","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, “combines fresh dates and bread.”"
"6484","Muhammad bin Muslim bin Wara Al-Razi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Wasiti told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yazid bin Al-Salt told us. On the authority of Muhammad, he is Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Roman, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “Eating watermelon with fresh dates” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6485","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: I am Isa, and he is Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the two dates to be combined.”"
"6486","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us with dates. Then Ibn Umar used to say: Do not compare, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade Quran, unless a man asks his brother’s permission.” Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad, on the authority of Khaled bin al-Harith, on the authority of Shu`bah, with a waqf mas'ar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6487","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad al-Harrani told us, saying: Immortal is the same as us. He said: Musa’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was asked “about the juxtaposition of dates,” and he said: “He should not juxtapose, unless he asks for permission.” \His companions\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6488","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abbas al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided seven dates among seven, and I am among them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6489","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “The example of a believer who reads the Qur’an is that of a citron. Its taste is good and its scent is pleasant, and the example of a believer who does not He recites the Qur’an, “It is like a date, its taste is good, but it has no odor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6490","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Al-Sa’q told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The example of a believer who reads the Qur’an is like a citrus fruit, its taste is good and its scent is pleasant, and the example of a believer who does not read the Qur’an is Like a date, its taste is good, but it has no odor.”"
"6491","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Uthman bin Omar told us. He said: I am Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir. He said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reaping disasters, and he said: “It is upon you.” With the black of it, for it is the best of it. We said: Were you herding sheep, O Messenger of God? He said: And there was no prophet who did not herd them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6492","Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Abi Sufyan informed me, that Amr bin Abdullah bin Safwan told him that Kalada bin al-Hanbal told him that Safwan bin Umayyah sent him to the conquest to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was at the top of the valley, and he said: I entered upon him, but I did not greet him, and he did not greet him. He asked for permission, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go back and say: Peace be upon you. Shall I come in?” That was after Safwan had converted to Islam. Amr said: Umayyah ibn Safwan also told me this news. Umayyah did not say: I heard it from Kalada. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6493","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Saeed bin Al-Huwayrith told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “defecated, then came out, ate, but did not touch water.”"
"6494","Muhammad bin Ubaid told me, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, “If he wanted to sleep while he was in his state of state, he would perform his ablution for prayer, and if he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6495","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to eat or sleep while he was in a state of ritual ablution, he would perform ablution."
"6496","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Suleiman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Samurah, he said: We were with the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We exchanged pages from morning until nightfall, ten would rise and ten would sit down. We said: What did she spread? ! He said: “What are you wondering about? It only came from here,” and he pointed with his hand to the sky. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6497","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sit at a table over which wine is being served,” and he once said Other: Or he said: “Alcohol is drunk on her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6498","Qutaibah told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for “I do not eat while reclining.”"
"6499","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abbas He said: Ibn Abbas was speaking, “God, Blessed and Most High, sent to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, an angel from the angels, and with him Gabriel, and the angel said: God gives you the choice between being a servant and a prophet, or being a king. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned. To Gabriel, like a counselor. Gabriel indicated with his hand: “Be humble.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, I will be the servant of a prophet.” He said: After that word, he did not eat food while reclining. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6500","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Musab bin Sulaym told us, he said: I heard Anas saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me Peace be upon him in his need, so I came to him and dates were given to him, and he began to eat while he was sitting down."
"6501","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and if If he drinks, let him drink with his right, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq. He said: I heard Malik speaking, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Like him. Muammar bin Rashid disagreed with him. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq. He said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Like him. Ibn Uyaynah said to Muammar: Al-Zuhri narrated it on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah. Muammar said: Al-Zuhri used to pronounce the hadith on the authority of the people. Perhaps he heard them all (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6502","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Omar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and if he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”"
"6503","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No “Eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand.”"
"6504","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his grandfather The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and if he drinks, let him drink with his right hand.” Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.” Ubayd Allah bin Sa`d bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. . . The same as him. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is a mistake, and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6505","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of His father, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, licking his three fingers of food."
"6506","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah “They did not put their hands in food until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had begun.”"
"6507","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abu Hudhayfah Al-Arhabi, on the authority of Hudhayfah, He said: When we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were invited to a meal, we would not lay down our hands until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it. He raised his hand, so we were invited to eat food, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not put down his hand, so we restrained ourselves, then a Bedouin came as if he were being chased away. So he leaned toward the bowl with his hand, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it by the hand and made him sit. Then a maid came and fell. with her hand to the bowl, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it by the hand, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Satan We were tired of leaving the remembrance of God on our food, so he brought this Bedouin to make our food lawful, so when we locked him up, he brought this slave girl. So that our food may be lawful with it, for by God, his hand is in my hand along with her hand.” Then he mentioned the name of God, and he ate."
"6508","Abdullah bin Al-Sabah bin Abdullah Al-Attar told me, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, that he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had food, so he said: “Come near, my son, and eat food.” God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” Khalid bin Al-Harith disagreed with him."
"6509","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, Khaled said in this hadith: A reading, on the authority of a man from Banu Sa’d, who His name was Al-Saadi. Al-Saadi narrated to him, on the authority of a man from Muzainah who was a neighbor of Omar bin Abi Salamah. Al-Muzani narrated that Omar mentioned that he came One day, there was food in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: “Sit down, my son, and give the name of God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is what is right with us, and God knows best, and God grants us success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6510","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “If a man enters his house and mentions God when he enters and when he eats food, Satan says: There is no room for the night, and there is no dinner.” Here for you, and when he entered and did not mention God when he entered, Satan said: Have you spent the night spending the night, even if he did not mention the name of God when he entered? His food. He said: “You have spent the night and dinner.”"
"6511","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Jabir bin Subh told us, he said: Muthanna bin Abdul Rahman Al-Khuza’i told me, He said: My grandfather Umayyah bin Makhshi, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw A man was eating and did not say Bismillah, so when he was taking his last bite, he said: In the name of God, the beginning and the end, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What Satan kept eating with him, so when he called, Satan vomited what he ate.”"
"6512","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, he said: I heard Wahb bin Kaysan, saying: I heard Omar bin Abu Salamah says: I was a boy in the lap of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my hand was wandering over the page, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “O boy, name God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you.” Malik ibn Anas disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6513","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym Wahb bin Kaysan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with food. And with him was his stepson, Omar bin Abi Salamah. He said to him: “Name God, and eat of what follows you.” This is more likely to be correct"
"6514","Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami told us, he said: Azhar Al-Samman told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Thumama told me, on the authority of Anas, he said “I went with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to the house of a master who had a tailor. He brought us a piece of cloth with lizards in it, and he started following that lizard.” He eats it, and I have continued to love wild animals since that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6515","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a bowl of porridge, and he said: “Eat from its sides, and do not eat from its middle, for the blessing You will descend in the midst of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6516","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, he said: Abdullah bin Secretly, he said: My father said to my mother: If you make food for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she made porridge, and he said with his hand: “Reduce,” so he set off. My father, so he called him, and he put his hand on its top, then he said: “Take in the name of God.” So they took something similar from him, and when they tasted it, he prayed for them. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, forgive them, have mercy on them, bless them, and provide for them. Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6517","Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, he said: Al-Azhar bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Secretly, he said: My mother said to my father: If we prepare food for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I called him, he said: So we did, so we prepared for him Porridge with ghee. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and entered the house. My mother placed some of her amaranth for him and collected it for him, so he sat. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on it, so we placed it for him. He said: “Take it in the name of God,” and he pointed to its top with three fingers. When he finished, we said: Pray for us, O Messenger of God. He said: O God, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless their livelihood."
"6518","Abu Bakr bin Nafi told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say: “When he ate food, he would lick his three fingers and say: If a morsel of any of you falls, let him remove any harm from it. And let him eat it and not leave it to Satan.”"
"6519","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz is Ibn Asad told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered us to scoop out the piece, for you do not know the blessing in which of your food lies.”"
"6520","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ja’far bin Amr bin told me. Umayyah, that his father, Amr ibn Umayyah, told him that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “grabbing the shoulder of a sheep in his hand.” So he was called To pray, he threw it and the knife he was holding, so he stood up and prayed, but he did not perform ablution, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6521","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, he said: Abu Zur’ah bin Amr told me. Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: Meat was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the arm was raised to him, and he liked it, so he gasped. \from it\"""""""
"6522","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If one of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand until he licks it, or he licks it, and he should not lift the plate until He licks it, or he licks it, for there is blessing in it at the end of the food.”"
"6523","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Salih bin Yahya, on the authority of his grandfather, Al-Muqaddam Ibn Maadi Karib Al-Kindi said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A human being filled a vessel worse than a stomach, according to the human being.” A few bites that strengthen his back, and if his soul overcomes it, then he mentions a word, meaning: one-third is food, one-third is drink, and one-third is for the soul. Baqiya bin Walid (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6524","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah Sulayman bin Sulaym, on the authority of Yahya bin Jabir, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Anguish, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No human being fills a vessel worse than a stomach. His soul overwhelmed him, so one third is food, one third is drink, and one third is for the soul.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6525","Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Muawiyah ibn Salih informed me, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Jabir, speaking about Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no vessel worse than a stomach. A Muslim is sufficient for food that strengthens his core. If it is unavoidable, then a third is for his food, a third for his drink, and a third for himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6526","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi` told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “The believer eats with one intestine, and the unbeliever eats with seven intestines.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6527","Amr bin Yazid Al-Basri told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Adi bin Thabit told me, he said: I heard Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: An infidel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he converted to Islam, so he began to eat a little, and this was before He eats a lot. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “The infidel eats with seven intestines, and the believer eats with \in one person\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6528","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Ali bin Shuaib Al-Baghdadi told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and the pronunciation To him, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The food for two is sufficient for three. “The food for three is sufficient for four.”"
"6529","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashar informed me, saying: Abdul Rahman told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The food of one is sufficient for two, the food of two is sufficient for four, and the food of four is sufficient for eight.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6530","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “None of you should wipe his hand until he licks it, or licks it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6531","Shuaib bin Yusuf Al-Naysaburi told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “When one of you eats, he should not wipe his hand with a napkin until he licks it, or licks it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6532","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abu Nu’aym, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “If a morsel falls from one of you, let him wipe out whatever harm has befallen it, let him eat it, and do not leave it for Satan, nor He wipes his hand with a napkin until he licks it, or he licks it, for he does not know which of his food is blessed.”"
"6533","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abi Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Wine itself was forbidden, whether small or large, and intoxicants of all kinds.” \drink\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6534","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam Al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Only wine itself was forbidden, and all intoxicants from every drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6535","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Abbas told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Abbas bin Dhuraih, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “Alcohol in itself was forbidden, whether it is small or much, and what “I am more intoxicated than any drink.”"
"6536","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and then does not repent from it, will be deprived of it in the Hereafter.” The wording is by Ibn al-Qasim"
"6537","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: I am Ibn Idris, on the authority of Zakaria, and Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard Umar, on the authority of From the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he says: “As for what follows, the prohibition on wine was revealed, and it is of five types: grapes, wheat, And barley, and dates, and honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6538","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, he said: Al-Sha’bi told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I heard Omar, delivering a sermon from the pulpit of the city, said: “O people, the prohibition of alcohol was revealed on the day it was revealed, and it is made from five types: grapes, And dates, and honey, and wheat, and barley, and wine: whatever the mind is dulled with.”"
"6539","Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: I am Abd al-Rahman, he said: Thana Shu’bah, and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, and the pronunciation for it, he said: Thana. Abdul Rahman, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: “Wine is from five: Of raisins, dates, barley, wheat, and honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6540","Hajib ibn Sulayman al-Munbiji told me, on the authority of Waki`, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: “Alcohol From five: dates, raisins, wheat, barley, and honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6541","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “ Wine is made from five things: dates, wheat, barley, honey, and grapes.”"
"6542","Ahmed bin Saeed told me, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told me, he said: I am Amr, and he is the son of Abi Qais, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Amer, who said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, of honey is wine, and of dates, there is wine. And of the raisins is wine, and of the wheat is wine, and of the barley is wine.”"
"6543","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Kathir told me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The wine is in these two trees: the palm tree and the grape.”"
"6544","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib Ibn Dathar, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: “ “Al-Basr and dates, wine.”"
"6545","Suwayd informed us, saying: 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Muharib, from Jabir, who said: ""Busru (unripe dates) and tamru (dried dates) are khamr (intoxicant)."""""
"6546","Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, that Anas bin Malik told them, he said: “While I was standing, in the neighborhood, and I The youngest of them in my family, when a man came and said: She has forbidden alcohol, and I am standing over them, giving them drink from what they had in abundance, and he said “I suffice for it,” so I sufficed for it, so I said to Anas: “What is it?” He said: “Burs and dates.” Abu Bakr bin Anas said: “It was their wine at that time.” Anas denies"
"6547","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a man from the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade dates, dates, raisins, and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6548","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Artaat, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the consumption of dried fruits, dates, raisins, and dates.”"
"6549","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Abdullah bin Abu Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not combine dates with raisins, nor combine fresh and fresh dates, and discard \Each one of them separately.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6550","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade mixing dates, raisins, and wine. Pride and pride are mixed, and pride and pride are mixed.”"
"6551","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He forbade a mixture of dates and raisins, and dates and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6552","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Kilab bin Ali, He told him that Abu Salamah told him, that Aisha told him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade mixing “Basr and rutab, and between raisins and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6553","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: I am Abu Amer, he said: Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Thumama bin Kilab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not avoid raisins and dates altogether, and do not avoid dates and dates altogether.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6554","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Uthman bin Omar told us, he said: Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not shun fresh dates and dates altogether, and do not shun raisins and dates altogether, but shun \Everyone individually\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6555","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said about the preposition that it should be discarded, and about dates and wheat that it should be mixed between them, and about dates and raisins that it should be mixed. \They get mixed up\"""""""
"6556","Muhammad bin Adam and Ali bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the mixture of dates and raisins, and the use of dates and raisins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6557","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, by reading, on the authority of Ata, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not combine dates and dates, nor raisins and dates.”"
"6558","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he forbade raisins to be discarded. And dates altogether, and he forbade the rejection of whole husks and dates.”"
"6559","On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of someone trustworthy in him. On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, both of them are trustworthy, and Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab, and in the hadith of al-Harith ibn Miskin: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith al-Ansari al-Sulami, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade drinking all dates and raisins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6560","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not shun fresh dates and fresh dates altogether, and do not shun fresh dates and raisins altogether, and shun \Each one of them individually.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6561","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he forbade abandoning Raisins and dates altogether, and he forbade the rejection of raisins and raisins altogether.”"
"6562","Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim Al-Abdi, he said: Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from mixing raisins with dates, or raisins with dates, or raisins with dates.”"
"6563","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6564","6573 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6565","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Hammad bin Hanbal told us. Zaid, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” Ahmed said: This is an authentic hadith."
"6566","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, and Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Thana Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the sale? He said: “Any drink that is intoxicating is forbidden.” In the hadith of Ma’mar, he said: “And a purchase of honey.”"
"6567","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf and Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"6568","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa told me, on the authority of his father, he said: He sent me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of God, there are drinks in it, so what should I drink, and what should I leave off? He said: “What are they?” He said: “Al-ba’at” and what is ale. He said: “And what is Al-B’at’, and what is an ale?” I said: “As for Al-Ba’at: it is honey wine, and as for ale: Then the corn wine, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not drink intoxicants, for I have forbidden every intoxicant.”"
"6569","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah Al-Jarmi, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, while he was leaning his back. To the Kaaba on the authority of Al-Badhiq, he said: “Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, preceded Al-Badhiq, and whatever intoxicates is forbidden,” and he said: I am the first of the Arabs. He asked him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6570","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir “that A man from two armies, and two armies from Yemen, came and asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a drink they drink in their land of corn. He is called : Bil, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Or is it an intoxicant? He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. God has entrusted to me, whoever drinks intoxicants, to give him to drink of the clay of vinegar. They said: O Messenger of God, and what is the clay of vinegar? He said: The sweat of the people Fire, or the juice of the people of Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6571","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man asked him “about Drinks, and he said: Avoid everything that causes intoxication."
"6572","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Amr bin Shuaib narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whatever in large amounts intoxicates, even a small amount of it is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6573","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The intoxicant, A little and a lot of it is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6574","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: A man came to Ibn Omar, and he said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, our family makes us drink in the evening, so when we wake up in the morning, we drink it. He said: “He forbids intoxicants.” Little and much, and I bear God’s witness, he forbade you from intoxicants. Little and much, and I bear God’s witness, he forbade you from Intoxicants, whether small or large, and I bear God’s witness to you, the people of Khaybar choose to drink from such-and-such, and call it such-and-such. It is wine, and the people of Fadak prefer to drink such-and-such, so they call it such-and-such, and it is wine, until he counted four. Drinks, one of which is honey.”"
"6575","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Tawus, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Nabeez al-Jar, and he said: Yes. Tawoos said: By God, I heard it from him."
"6576","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: he told me Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade jars, mounts, and fake envelopes.”"
"6577","Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Asma’, the daughter of Yazid, on the authority of a cousin of hers, called: Anas, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Didn’t God say: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it? I said: Yes, he said: Didn’t God say: It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should have any choice. Order them? He said: I said: Yes, he said: I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the hornbill, the hornbill, the lizard, and the lizard.”"
"6578","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muharib, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “Peace be upon him, on the authority of the woods, the hantams, and the imitated ones.”"
"6579","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik that he told him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said, “He forbade animals that are scavengers, and that they should be shunned.”"
"6580","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aisha: What Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid it from containers? She said: “He forbade the use of carpets and imitated earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6581","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ibrahim, speaking on the authority of Al-Aswad said: I said to Aisha: What containers did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid? She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of carpets and imitated earth.”"
"6582","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah and Sufyan told us, and he said another time: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, Suleiman, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade scavengers. And she said again: “And the fake one.”"
"6583","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, Hammad, and Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of saddlebags and imitated stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6584","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdul Khaleq Al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrating, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the lizards, the hantam, and the hornbill.” Shu’bah said: The mention of asphalt is mentioned by no one other than Ibn Umar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6585","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Aban bin Yazid told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn al-Musayyab and Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered them to With four, and he forbade them from four: “He forbade them from drinking in Al-Hantam, Al-Dabba’, Al-Naqir, and Al-Mzafat. They said: What shall we drink from?” He said: “You must drink water from human beings, and those on whose mouths are licked.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6586","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa`id, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a delegation Abd Qais, on the authority of the Dabba’, the Hantam, the Naqir, and the Muzaffat, to stand apart therein.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6587","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Harith, he said: We sat with a man called: Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab, so they mentioned to him the hadith of Ibn Umar regarding the genitive, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not forbid it, but his companions fell into Jarrar Khaybar, and he forbade them from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6588","Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri was asked about He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade wine that is brought to you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yahya bin Sa’id disagreed with him."
"6589","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Alaniyah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the wine of wine.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Alaniyah al-Sahib, who He made a mistake before him, and God knows best. He changed it with Yazid bin Abi Saeed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6590","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb told me, he said: I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He told me Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the wine of draft.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6591","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Hussein, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Abdullah bin Omar narrated to me, that Omar “forbade the wine of preposition”"
"6592","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of strong wine.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, without this wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6593","Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, so he told us about Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade moving creatures and imitated things.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6594","Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6595","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Khaythamah told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he is the son of Abd al-Warith bin Saeed, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Juhadah, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Utba bin Farqad, he said: “The wine that Omar drank it, it became corrupted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6596","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, that He told him that Omar went out to them and said: “I smelled the scent of alcohol from so-and-so, and he claimed that he drank paint, and I am asking what he drank. He was drunk, I flogged him, and he was flogged for the full life of punishment.”"
"6597","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “He was the most beloved The drink was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sweet and cold.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6598","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: “Abdullah was brought a drink, and he said: Give it to Alqamah, he said: I am fasting, he said: Give me the black one, he said: I am fasting, he said: I am fasting. So-and-so said: I am fasting. They all said: I am fasting. Abdullah said: I am not fasting. So he took a drink and then said: They fear a day when hearts and eyes will be transformed."
"6599","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: “People make people drink, I don’t know what it is, and I have not had a drink for twenty years, or he said: forty years, except “Water and berries,” but he did not mention wine. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6600","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, he said: Thumama bin Hazn Al-Qushayri told us, he said: I met Aisha So I asked her about wine, and she called an Ethiopian maid, and she said: Ask this woman, for she used to recite wine for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Ethiopian woman said: “I used to bow down to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the night, and I would tie him up and hang him up, and when the morning came, \drank\"""""""
